## Impact
There is no way to remove derivative and even if the owner will set weight = 0 it will not help (it does not remove a protocol address from derivatives mapping).
If one protocol from derivatives will be compromised it is still will be called in [unstake()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-03-asymmetry/blob/main/contracts/SafEth/SafEth.sol#L118) function and will be reverted everytime. 
the impossibility of removing a bad protocol from derivatives may cause all funds to get stuck on the derivative addresses.

