# Vulnerability details

When staking, the total amount of `SafEth` is calculated through a weight system. Each derivative can have a different weight:

```solidity
uint256 totalStakeValueEth = 0; // total amount of derivatives worth of ETH in system
for (uint i = 0; i < derivativeCount; i++) {
    uint256 weight = weights[i];
    IDerivative derivative = derivatives[i];
    if (weight == 0) continue;
    uint256 ethAmount = (msg.value * weight) / totalWeight;

    // This is slightly less than ethAmount because slippage
    uint256 depositAmount = derivative.deposit{value: ethAmount}();
    uint derivativeReceivedEthValue = (derivative.ethPerDerivative(
        depositAmount
    ) * depositAmount) / 10 ** 18;
    totalStakeValueEth += derivativeReceivedEthValue;
}
// mintAmount represents a percentage of the total assets in the system
uint256 mintAmount = (totalStakeValueEth * 10 ** 18) / preDepositPrice;
_mint(msg.sender, mintAmount);
```

The owner can modify the weight for a specific derivative anytime by calling the `adjustWeight` function. It's possible to deactivate a derivative by setting its weight to zero:

```solidity
function adjustWeight(
    uint256 _derivativeIndex,
    uint256 _weight
) external onlyOwner {
    weights[_derivativeIndex] = _weight;
    uint256 localTotalWeight = 0;
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < derivativeCount; i++)
        localTotalWeight += weights[i];
    totalWeight = localTotalWeight;
    emit WeightChange(_derivativeIndex, _weight);
}
```

However, it's also possible to set all weights to zero. If this happens, a user wouldn't receive any `SafEth` when staking, because `totalStakeValueEth` would be zero, thus all funds deposited would be stuck inside the contract.

