## Impact
Detailed description of the impact of this finding.
This is a medium risk as it is controlled by the owner and it is assumed that owner will operate in good faith.

But, if by mistake if the owner of the contract adds a new derivative to this contract with invalid address or something incomplete, this mistake can impact the whole functioning of the contracts.
Since the array of derivatives is used in the process of staking, re balancing, any incorrect additional will impact all these functions.

The difficult part is the inability to remove the entry added by mistake. Once this mistake is committed, the contract becomes unusable.

